WEBVTT

00:00:00.052 --> 00:00:06.279
This is the running SlothLab app. The selected investigation was completed earlier; this walkthrough does not start a new research run.

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:12.463
Switch between Light, Dark, and System appearance.

00:00:12.463 --> 00:00:19.227
New investigation defines a testable question within the registered prior-correction experiment.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:24.419
Discover installed models on a local or remote Ollama-compatible endpoint. Experiments still execute on the app host.

00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:31.461
Set experiment and token budgets before running. Reserve independent confirmation seeds. No new investigation is launched in this recording.

00:00:31.461 --> 00:00:38.425
The completed investigation contains five real executions and one verified reuse. These are recorded results, not simulated demo data.

00:00:38.425 --> 00:00:45.384
Inspect the experiment table and distinguish execution from exact-result reuse. Reuse does not count as independent replication.

00:00:45.384 --> 00:00:54.033
Read the finite protocol assessment and confirmatory evidence. Operational completion does not establish a universal scientific conclusion.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:01:00.639
Prepare and download a portable research bundle containing recorded measurements and artifacts.

00:01:00.639 --> 00:01:07.986
Guest mode uses temporary JSON documents and artifact files. Download a bundle to preserve the session.

00:01:07.986 --> 00:01:14.986
The exported investigation is now reopened in Guest mode. Importing history starts no inference.

00:01:14.986 --> 00:01:20.899
Learn and help provides a captioned lesson, chapter navigation, transcripts, and practice questions.

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:29.734
Use the checklist to plan hypotheses, controls, confirmation seeds, budgets, and uncertainty.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:35.825
A named local browser profile keeps separate history on this browser and origin. It is a convenience profile, not cross-device account sign-in.
